<title>SWEDEN: Ericsson wins Singapore taxi radio deal.</title>
<headline>Ericsson wins Singapore taxi radio deal.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish telecoms group LM Ericsson AB said on Monday it had received an order for 3,000 Mobitex radio modems from Comfort Taxi in Singapore.</p>
<p>The financial details of the contract were not released.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that Comfort Taxi was expanding its Cablink system, developed by CEI Technologies, which involved computerised tracking and dispatching.</p>
<p>Ericsson said currently half of Comfort's fleet of 10,000 taxis were equipped with Cablink and this order would lift the number to 8,000.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
